## Evidence Standards

- Separate code facts, observations, interpretations, hypotheses, proposed methods, and conclusions.
- Smoke runs and reduced paths are engineering evidence only; label them and list what they omit.
- Open and inspect representative images before any spatial, rendering, or visual claim.
- Raw outputs, logs, caches, and checkpoints stay in <persistent store>; Git holds reviewed analysis and
  representative evidence.
- Report `completed`, `not done`, `skipped`, `deferred`, and `blocked` items explicitly.

## Stop and Ask

<!-- The Codex patch: its default is to keep going until the task is resolved. Name the checkpoints. -->

Stop and ask the user before:

- choosing between research directions, methods, or baselines;
- changing model, data, loss, training, or evaluation semantics beyond the written plan;
- creating environments, downloading large models, or launching GPU or paid jobs;
- promoting an exploration result to a decision, default, or milestone.

Decide engineering details yourself (file layout, helper names, test scaffolding) and record them in the
ledger.

